{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011oUS5BtCCvXtNNpuXVD1gh","type":"tool_result","content":"1020:- `shots.burst(base, vels)`: fire several at once from a pattern list of [vx, v2] (v2 = vy on the ground plane, vz in side view)\n1021:- `shots.clear(team)`: remove every bullet, or only one team's\n1022:- `shots.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (glowing cores, or their sprites)\n1023:- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n1024:- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits\n1025:- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n1026:- `shots.list = []`: the live bullets\n1027:- `shots.max`: at most this many at once\n1028:- `shots.plane`: 'ground' (they fly over x and y) or 'side' (x and z)\n1029:- `shots.sparks`: a puff of sparks where one hits a wall\n80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase).\n1003:- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n1004:- `suspicion.reset()` †: back to calm\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1006:- `suspicion.alert = 1`, `suspicion.notice = .3`, `suspicion.search = .65` †: the levels where each state starts\n1007:- `suspicion.changed = false` †: the state changed this step\n1008:- `suspicion.decay = .3`, `suspicion.rise = 1.5` †: per second\n1009:- `suspicion.forget = 6` †: seconds an alert guard searches after losing the target\n1010:- `suspicion.last = null` †: where it last saw or heard the target ({ x, y, z }), or null\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184349__x8b64cc/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b59097-524b-47da-837f-b83180a4d05e","uuid":"e703b7b4-e2c1-4373-bb63-d2ab62cfd458","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:48:39.267Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1020:- `shots.burst(base, vels)`: fire several at once from a pattern list of [vx, v2] (v2 = vy on the ground plane, vz in side view)\n1021:- `shots.clear(team)`: remove every bullet, or only one team's\n1022:- `shots.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (glowing cores, or their sprites)\n1023:- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n1024:- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits\n1025:- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n1026:- `shots.list = []`: the live bullets\n1027:- `shots.max`: at most this many at once\n1028:- `shots.plane`: 'ground' (they fly over x and y) or 'side' (x and z)\n1029:- `shots.sparks`: a puff of sparks where one hits a wall\n80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase).\n1003:- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n1004:- `suspicion.reset()` †: back to calm\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1006:- `suspicion.alert = 1`, `suspicion.notice = .3`, `suspicion.search = .65` †: the levels where each state starts\n1007:- `suspicion.changed = false` †: the state changed this step\n1008:- `suspicion.decay = .3`, `suspicion.rise = 1.5` †: per second\n1009:- `suspicion.forget = 6` †: seconds an alert guard searches after losing the target\n1010:- `suspicion.last = null` †: where it last saw or heard the target ({ x, y, z }), or null\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184349__x8b64cc/work","interrupted":false