{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfBjWeHZPz4Myq2e7CfA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything passes, so I'm writing the exit interview now. I'll use one JSON file as the source for the in-game About screen and the root `exit-interview.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1756,"cache_read_input_tokens":272435,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1756,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b59097-524b-47da-837f-b83180a4d05e","uuid":"b37a5565-acfd-4bad-8442-dc0569c0a006","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:13:34.730Z","request_id":"req_011CgfBjWEy4dZPGvsZE7kYz"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfBjWeHZPz4Myq2e7CfA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GnhE7Ct2YQtBpFmkZT4omX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nd={\n\"sourceInformation\":{\n \"date\":\"2026-11-02 18:43\",\n \"source\":\"Breaking Bad (2008-2013)\",\n \"genre\":\"Action-stealth with crafting minigames (the cook, the laundry), gang shootouts and a boss fight\",\n \"perspective\":\"Three-quarter top-down (the engine's threequarter view); the player can switch to top-down or isometric\",\n \"tech\":\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (handoff package, full engine, unmodified, inlined into one HTML file); AI Hub session client 1.3.0 inlined; plain JavaScript, no other libraries\",\n \"artDirection\":\"The engine's native HD-pixel look: 320x240-minimum expanding screen, textured TileMap walls and floors, code-drawn props and shapes, Humanoid rigs with outfits, canvas lighting that darkens toward dusk\",\n \"animation\":\"The engine's native system: procedural Humanoid rigs, E.Attack wrench swings, poses and expressions, particles and hit effects\",\n \"audio\":\"All in code: chip-synth music per scene (title twang, town with a chase layer, cook ostinato, boss, desk) and sound effects; Animalese-style gibberish voices, one pitch per speaker, no recorded audio\",\n \"online\":\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1 to 4 players: each copy sends its player's position about 8 times a second and shows the others' characters; nothing else is sent\",\n \"testing\":\"Headless Chromium and WebKit through Playwright: smoke runs, a scripted full playthrough (teleports plus key presses), the attract-mode loop, the AI Hub harness (2 and 4 players, latency and loss, host-leave), a fake DualSense for glyph and axis-flip checks, screenshots at phone, tablet, desktop and ultrawide sizes. No real controller and no real iOS Safari\",\n \"research\":\"None beyond the engine docs and the AI Hub protocol; the tone comes from general knowledge of the show, and the story is an original riff\",\n \"environment\":\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n \"model\":\"Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n \"usage\":\"unknown (token and cost estimates are not exposed to the session)\"},\n\"testingFeedback\":[\n \"Seven: every enemy deleted each frame (E.prune used backwards), a missing middle-dot glyph shown as '?', a title menu overlapping the characters, the cook's demo AI missing its heat band, hit notes drawn past the line, the Controller toggles landing on the Controls screen instead of Settings, and a shared test port that served another run's game to the hub harness.\",\n \"One: the E.prune mistake, which left the world with no cops, goons or boss, so the game could not be played or finished.\",\n \"The attract-mode soak plus a scripted full playthrough with debug snapshots: it drove the cook, the laundry, the fight and the boss through the real scenes and printed the state at each step; the AI Hub harness came a close second.\",\n \"Static screenshots of the title at several viewport sizes: they found no layout problems, because the engine's expand mode already handled every shape.\"],\n\"engineFeedback\":[\n \"The look comes almost free: cutaway TileMap walls, shaded Humanoid rigs with outfits, materials, canvas lighting and particles, plus the pause menu, settings, controls rebinding, dialog with portraits and the HTML HUD, so the time went into design and not plumbing. The fixed step made headless, repeatable tests easy.\",\n \"Yes. E.prune removes the items the callback returns true for, which I read as keep. A one-line index entry was not enough there. Settings in the 'Controller' group show on the Controls screen and not Settings, and the font has no middle dot. I also guessed that the dialog voice could be per speaker; it takes one effect name, so I read the text as it types and play my own blips.\",\n \"The game's brain: the story as scripts over dialog, the cop's sight and suspicion, the goons and the boss's telegraphed charge, the cook and laundry minigames, the attract-mode AI that plays through them, the gibberish voices, the stick-flip patch for the Settings toggles, the touch-only notice and the AI Hub ghost sync.\",\n \"Working out what a call means from one line: prune's direction, the dialog's internals for typed-text sounds, and which direction a screen vector becomes on the ground in each view when an AI has to steer.\",\n \"The prune helper: rename it removeIf or make the predicate a keep test, so the call reads like what it does.\",\n \"Give every game a debug handle on window by default (the scene, the state snapshot, a go() and a teleport), because every browser test had to add one by hand.\"],\n\"promptFeedback\":[\n \"A single clear goal with concrete done checks (attract mode after 10 seconds, the 10-foot controller philosophy, the hub protocol, the exit-interview file) and freedom to choose the genre. The random title step made the name a small, fun commitment.\",\n \"'Engine native perspectives' for a 2D engine's views, and what the source's subject (a drug trade) should mean in a game: I kept the cook abstract and chemistry-free. The file name pattern with the source's name in it, and which folder the files go in, took a second read.\",\n \"Fitting a whole vertical slice (title, attract, story, three minigames, combat, boss, settings, About, hub) into one pass, and checking the controller experience without a pad in hand.\",\n \"A real DualSense played on a TV across a room for fifteen minutes, to judge aiming, prompts and the stick-flip toggles by feel.\"]\n}\nd[\"aiHub\"]={\n \"name\":\"Brewing Bad\",\n \"tagline\":\"Do the math. Cook the blue.\",\n \"description\":\"A spiritual successor to Breaking Bad: a chemistry teacher with nine weeks of insurance cooks, sells and launders his way past patrols, rival gangs and a boss. Stealth, shootouts and three minigames in a desert town.\",\n \"type\":\"Game\",\n \"genre\":\"Stealth\",\n \"source\":\"Breaking Bad\",\n \"series\":\"\",\n \"players\":\"1–4\",\n \"controls\":\"Move WASD or left stick; aim with mouse or right stick; wrench click, J or Square; flask right click, K or R2; use E or Cross; sprint Shift or L1; V changes the camera\",\n \"tags\":[\"3d\",\"story\",\"stealth\",\"comedy\",\"boss fights\",\"exploration\"]}\njson.dump(d,open('exit-interview.json','w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\njson.load(open('exit-interview.json')); print('ok', len(open('exit-interview.json').read()))\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1756,"cache_read_input_tokens":272435,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1756,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b59097-524b-47da-837f-b83180a4d05e","uuid":"d7a8b448-093e-44e1-8ee3-73dedab402f2","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:13:54.095Z","request_id":"req_011CgfBjWEy4dZPGvsZE7kYz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GnhE7Ct2YQtBpFmkZT4omX":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184349__x8b64cc/work && python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nd={\n\"sourceInformation\":{\n \"date\":\"2026-11-02 18:43\",\n \"source\":\"Breaking Bad (2008-2013)\",\n \"genre\":\"Action-stealth with crafting minigames (the cook, the laundry), gang shootouts and a boss fight\",\n \"perspective\":\"Three-quarter top-down (the engine's threequarter view); the player can switch to top-down or isometric\",\n \"tech\":\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (handoff package, full engine, unmodified, inlined into one HTML file); AI Hub session client 1.3.0 inlined; plain JavaScript, no other libraries\",\n \"artDirection\":\"The eng